; Toy robustness property for 2D classification
; Property: If input X is within [0.05, 0.15] for both dimensions,
; the output class should be 1 (meaning Y_1 > Y_0).
; In VNN-LIB, we specify the negation of the property to find counterexamples.
; So we specify: (Y_0 >= Y_1)

; Declare input variables (X_0, X_1)
(declare-const X_0 Real)
(declare-const X_1 Real)

; Declare output variables (Y_0, Y_1)
(declare-const Y_0 Real)
(declare-const Y_1 Real)

; Define input constraints (epsilon box)
(assert (>= X_0 -5.0))
(assert (<= X_0 5.0))
(assert (>= X_1 -5.0))
(assert (<= X_1 5.0))

; Define negated property to find counterexamples
; We want to prove Y_1 > Y_0. The negation is Y_0 >= Y_1
(assert (>= Y_0 Y_1))
